{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01106",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 4.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.16,
      "end_seconds": 8.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.51,
      "end_seconds": 13.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.89,
      "end_seconds": 17.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.69,
      "end_seconds": 21.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "It's been going on for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.89,
      "end_seconds": 32.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "So, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.37,
      "end_seconds": 39.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "It's a couple of times a week. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.79,
      "end_seconds": 44.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.81,
      "end_seconds": 48.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "It usually comes with stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.02,
      "end_seconds": 62.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "A few quick ones: vomiting or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.73,
      "end_seconds": 67.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.45,
      "end_seconds": 71.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Right, any recent antibiotics or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.24,
      "end_seconds": 75.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.23,
      "end_seconds": 83.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.48,
      "end_seconds": 86.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.38,
      "end_seconds": 91.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.85,
      "end_seconds": 96.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, you know, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.81,
      "end_seconds": 101.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "So, do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.0,
      "end_seconds": 110.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "something called glyc... Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.21,
      "end_seconds": 115.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.67,
      "end_seconds": 128.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. ORS. I take it a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.05,
      "end_seconds": 145.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.09,
      "end_seconds": 153.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Yes, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.19,
      "end_seconds": 156.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.96,
      "end_seconds": 174.46,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. Nothing, I'm teetotal. I swim twice a week. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.66,
      "end_seconds": 179.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.75,
      "end_seconds": 183.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "I've had diabetes, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.16,
      "end_seconds": 190.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.76,
      "end_seconds": 193.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "My son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.33,
      "end_seconds": 200.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Alright, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.29,
      "end_seconds": 203.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.81,
      "end_seconds": 224.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.64,
      "end_seconds": 236.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.73,
      "end_seconds": 265.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Okay: temp 38.3 degrees, respiratory rate 16. And pulse is 107 beats a minute, blood pressure 123 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.62,
      "end_seconds": 271.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Alright, I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.53,
      "end_seconds": 275.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.92,
      "end_seconds": 295.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Bowel sounds are active, tummy is soft with mild tenderness all around."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.99,
      "end_seconds": 298.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.06,
      "end_seconds": 313.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "You're mildly dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.33,
      "end_seconds": 330.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.8,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. From what you've told me and what I found, it points towards acute gastroenteritis. Another possibility is an infective colitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.64,
      "end_seconds": 334.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.38,
      "end_seconds": 364.0,
      "duration_seconds": 28.62,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's acute gastroenteritis, and we'll know more once the a stool test is back. We should do a stool test for diarrhoea. The treatment will be zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day, for ten days. That should help with diarrhoea. Stick to bananas, rice, toast, curd, and avoid milk and oily food till it settles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.42,
      "end_seconds": 375.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.02,
      "end_seconds": 378.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.43,
      "end_seconds": 395.32,
      "duration_seconds": 15.89,
      "text": "Let's hold off on blood salts for now, and if there's no change in two weeks we can revisit it. I'd like to see you again in three days. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.08,
      "end_seconds": 398.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}